+---
+title: 'RC1.2: Attestation UI — the References Section Choice'
+type: 'feature'
+created: '2026-08-01'
+status: 'done'
+baseline_commit: 'f04aff35715f2a3270517f609e7d810aa1a81b1a'
+review_loop_iteration: 0
+context: []
+---
+
+<frozen-after-approval reason="human-owned intent — do not modify unless human renegotiates">
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** RC1.1 made `reference_contact_choice` mandatory at submission, but the SSR application form renders no control for it — develop's form is unsubmittable. Applicants must see the References-section framing (UX §5.2), the attestation card (§5.3), and the Yes-path confirmation line (§5.4), all verbatim.
+
+**Approach:** Add the §5.2 framing copy to the References section (replacing the now-contradicted old section hint), render a `reference_attestation` card module at the end of the section (consent-block anatomy, required radio pair posting `reference_contact_choice=attested|declined`, no default), extract the RC1.1 inline choice check into one callable `validate_choice` function, and thread the attested flag to the confirmation page for the §5.4 line.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Copy verbatim from UX §5.2/§5.3/§5.4 (also §10.1 copy deck) — never paraphrased. Attestation/acknowledgement vocabulary only; the word "consent" never appears in relation to this record (AD-2).
+- Card anatomy per §5.3: heading "Contacting your referees", body copy with inline privacy link "How we handle referee data ↗" → `/privacy` (new tab, `noopener noreferrer`, same pattern as the existing notice-block link), radio pair with per-option label + description, anti-coercion footer.
+- Radio pair: `name="reference_contact_choice"`, values `attested`/`declined` (RC1.1's fixed server contract), required, **no default selection**, re-selects from `values` on error re-render.
+- A11y (UX §12): `role="radiogroup"` + `aria-required="true"` on the group, `aria-labelledby` → the card heading, help text linked via `aria-describedby`; error announced on submit-scroll (role="alert" span, same pattern as `view_radio_group`); `data-testid`s `ref-attestation` / `ref-attestation-yes` / `ref-attestation-no`.
+- Card carries `id="field-reference_contact_choice"` so the existing error-summary anchor (`error_summary.anchor_for`) scrolls to it; error state adds `has-error` + inline message "Choose one option to continue." (§5.3, already the RC1.1 server string).
+- Validation wiring = one self-contained public function (`reference_attestation.validate_choice(values)`) that `application_handler.validate_form` delegates to — the stepper (`form-stepper-f1`) will lift this same function into its References-step gating on rebase. No step-aware gating built here.
+- No-JS: plain SSR radios post with the multipart submission and persist via the RC1.1 path — no JS wiring added.
+- §5.4 confirmation line renders only when the persisted submission choice is `attested`; "No" and bot-trap (honeypot/timing) renders show nothing.
+- Old section hint ("Your landlord will ring every reference you list — please fill them all in.") is replaced by the §5.2 intro: the §10.1 copy deck defines §5.2 as *the* "References section intro", and the old line contradicts the feature (RightTenantry contacts referees on the Yes path). Flagged in the PR.
+
+**Ask First:**
+- Any change to field-level helper copy inside the referee groups (e.g. "Your landlord will ring them…" in the landlord group) — out of the AC scope; left as-is, flagged as an open question in the PR.
+- Any new schema, SQL, or Squirrel changes (none are needed — RC1.1 owns the write path).
+
+**Never:**
+- No "consent" wording, no opt-out checkbox, no default/pre-selected radio, no nag/re-ask on the declined path, no score treatment.
+- No stepper/multi-step work, no client-side JS changes (`form.js` untouched), no changes to RC1.1's persistence behavior (validate extraction is behavior-preserving).
+- No referee-specific privacy-policy section (counsel-pack dependency, launch-gating not build-gating); the link targets `/privacy`.
+- Never merge the PR; never commit env files/secrets.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Pristine render | no values | Card renders with all §5.3 copy, both radios unchecked, no error | N/A |
+| No selection at submit | field absent/empty | `validate_choice` → `#("reference_contact_choice", "Choose one option to continue.")`; re-render shows banner anchor → card with inline error + `has-error` | Server-side only (form has `novalidate`) |
+| Tampered value | value ∉ {attested, declined} | Same as missing (RC1.1 contract, incl. insert-layer abort) | 500 + log if it ever reaches insert |
+| Yes selected, error elsewhere | values carry `attested` | Re-render re-checks the Yes radio | N/A |
+| Yes submission | `attested` persists | Confirmation page carries the §5.4 line verbatim | N/A |
+| No submission | `declined` persists | Confirmation page shows NO §5.4 line; submits normally | N/A |
+| Bot-trap render | honeypot/timing | Spam confirmation page unchanged (no §5.4 line, no analytics) | N/A |
+
+</frozen-after-approval>
