+- Given no option selected at submit, when validation runs, then the error summary anchors to the card and the card shows "Choose one option to continue." with `has-error`.
+- Given a Yes submission, when the confirmation page renders, then it carries the §5.4 line verbatim; the No path and bot-trap renders show no such line.
+- Given JS unavailable, when the form posts, then the choice persists per RC1.1 (plain radios in the multipart POST).
+- Given any code/copy/comment naming this record, when reviewed, then attestation/acknowledgement vocabulary is used — never "consent".
+
+## Spec Change Log
+
+- **Trigger (review round 1):** blind-hunter — every bug-hunt scenario that submits `/apply` fails post-merge (none select `reference_contact_choice`; the label-invariants classification rejects the new required radio); edge-hunter + blind-hunter — `validate_choice` read the untrimmed `common.get_val` while the insert/acknowledgement paths read the trimming `get_form_value`, so validator and writer disagreed on crafted whitespace values. **Amended (non-frozen sections):** Code Map + Tasks gained the five scenario files; `validate_choice` trims; handler insert/acknowledgement sites adopt the module's `field_name`/`attested_value` constants; tests hardened (banner-label asserted as the full "label — message" row; `string.crop` ordering assertions guard anchor presence first); error span gains an id and joins `aria-describedby` on error; dead `attestation-block` class dropped. **Known-bad state avoided:** `/apply` E2E red on develop after merge; a posted `" attested "` rejected by validation yet acceptable to the writer. **KEEP:** verbatim copy constants in `form_copy`; consent-block card anatomy + radiogroup aria wiring; no default selection, ever; `validate_choice` as the single self-contained callable the stepper lifts; confirmation line on the attested path only.
+
+## Design Notes
+
+- `view_consent_block` does not exist as a function — the "anatomy" is the `.consent-block` elevated-card treatment in `review_consent.gleam` (card div + inner + `has-error` border). The attestation card reuses that treatment, not a shared function.
+- The existing `view_radio_group` helper can't express per-option descriptions or `aria-labelledby`/describedby wiring — the card builds its own radios, keeping the helper untouched.
+- Radio input ids follow the `field-<name>-<value>` convention (`field-reference_contact_choice-attested`/`-declined`) so any future per-option anchoring stays consistent.
+- `validate_choice` returns `Result(Nil, #(String, String))`; `validate_form` prepends the tuple on Error — identical ordering to RC1.1's inline block (error list order unchanged, `first_error_field` analytics unaffected).
+
+## Verification
+
+**Commands:**
+- `make test-server` -- green (render + validation + confirmation tests; RC1.1 handler tests still pass)
+- `make test` -- green repo-wide
+- `make build` -- compiles
+- `cd server && gleam format --check src test` -- formatting clean
+
+**Manual checks (if no CLI):**
+- `git grep -in "consent" -- server/src/application/form_sections/reference_attestation.gleam server/src/application/form_copy.gleam` returns nothing user-facing (vocabulary sweep; the `.consent-block` CSS anatomy class and the doc comment naming the rule itself are the only permitted mentions).
+- Rendered card HTML contains `role="radiogroup"`, `aria-required="true"`, `aria-describedby`, all three testids, and zero `checked` attributes on first paint.
+
+## Suggested Review Order
+
+**The card (the story's core)**
+
+- One module owns render + validation; the stepper lifts `validate_choice` unchanged.
+  [`reference_attestation.gleam:44`](../../server/src/application/form_sections/reference_attestation.gleam#L44)
+
+- Radiogroup aria wiring, no-default radios, error joins `aria-describedby` on error.
+  [`reference_attestation.gleam:59`](../../server/src/application/form_sections/reference_attestation.gleam#L59)
+
+- All applicant-facing strings verbatim from UX §5.2/§5.3/§5.4 — never paraphrase.
+  [`form_copy.gleam:27`](../../server/src/application/form_copy.gleam#L27)
+
+**Placement in the form**
+
+- §5.2 intro replaces the pre-v1 hint (copy deck defines it as THE section intro).
+  [`references.gleam:54`](../../server/src/application/form_sections/references.gleam#L54)
+
+- Card always closes the References section; posts with the plain SSR form.
+  [`references.gleam:236`](../../server/src/application/form_sections/references.gleam#L236)
+
+**Validation & submission wiring**
+
+- `validate_form` delegates — identical error ordering to RC1.1's inline block.
+  [`application_handler.gleam:525`](../../server/src/application/application_handler.gleam#L525)
+
+- Attested flag derived from posted values, threaded to the confirmation page.
+  [`application_handler.gleam:2150`](../../server/src/application/application_handler.gleam#L2150)
+
+- §5.4 line renders only when attested; bot-trap renders pass False.
+  [`form_pages.gleam:179`](../../server/src/application/form_pages.gleam#L179)
+
+**Presentation**
+
+- Consent-block card treatment + stacked 44px option rows, amber-checked state.
